# Centralized IPOPT timing sweep

When working on the centralized timing reconstruction, follow
`ddp/notes/CENTRALIZED_IPOPT_TIMING_SWEEP.md` exactly.

- Work on `ddp-understanding-sep02`; do not add results to an older branch.
- Use `scripts/run_centralized_ipopt_case.ps1`; do not edit `config.jl`.
- Run one cold-start IPOPT case at a time and preserve failure logs.
- A row is publishable only after accepted status and `FEASIBLE` validation.
- Record IPOPT, JuMP, and wall time separately; paper `C (s)` uses JuMP solve
  time.
- After every case, update, commit, and push MultiPeriodDistOPF first, then
  update, compile, verify, commit, and push the TPEC paper.
- Never launch the next case until both repositories contain the preceding row.
